{
  "$comment": [
    "The SDS migration mapping: each old value and what replaces it, per use. Codemods, lint autofix suggestions and agents read it, so a mapping is decided once, here.",
    "colors[].by is keyed by the use a value is put to, as the scanner reads it from the receiving key: fg (text, icons, tints), bg (a fill), bgPressed (a fill in a pressed state), stroke (a border), line (the fill of a View one pixel thin), placeholder (placeholderTextColor). A use not listed falls back: line to stroke, bgPressed to bg, placeholder to fg; mixed or unknown uses have no mapping and stay manual.",
    "next: the replacement (a role fg.*/bg.*/stroke.*, a palette static value, an SdsSpacing/SdsRadius token, a type step t1..t13, or a Txt fontWeight), or null when nothing replaces it yet (reason says why). byContext: the replacement depends on what the site draws, named by context; a codemod leaves those to a person.",
    "exact: the light value is identical (CIEDE2000 under 0.5; for byContext, every candidate is), so a K batch can move it with no visual change. needsVerification: the site changes on screen or needs a human choice, so it ships in a V or H batch with screenshots.",
    "decision: the inventory decision (05-sds-migration-inventory.md section 5.1, approved 2026-10-10) that set this mapping.",
    "scripts/codemods/sds/migration-map.test.mjs checks every next against the token files."
  ],
  "decisions": {
    "D-grey500-text": "grey500 text and icons move to fg.neutralSubtle: a step darker, and contrast rises",
    "D-grey400-text": "grey400 text and icons move to fg.placeholder: a step darker",
    "D-grey800-text": "grey800 text moves to fg.neutral",
    "D-white-label": "white text takes the on*Solid role of the fill beneath; over a photo or video it stays static white",
    "D-brand-fill": "a brand fill moves to bg.brandSolid",
    "D-grey-fill": "a screen or section ground is bg.layerBasement; a control such as a button or chip is bg.neutralWeak",
    "off-scale-type": "10px text folds to t1 (11px); no step is added"
  },
